Subject: Re: [PATCH v2] fs/ntfs3: fix double ni_unlock() in ntfs_readdir()
In-Reply-To: <20261029052102.1585462-1-christian.aurichzm@gmail.com>
References: <20261029052102.1585462-1-christian.aurichzm@gmail.com>

On Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:21:02 -0300, Christian Aurich Zanettini Martins wrote:
> This also happens when getdents64() fills the supplied buffer,
> triggering a lockdep "bad unlock balance" warning.
>
> Jump to out_free instead to avoid unlocking an already released lock.

I hit the same warning while testing ntfs3 master (ee1cb3443cff) with
lockdep in a QEMU/KVM guest: "ls -f" of a 3000-entry directory, 20
times, with concurrent stat(2) calls, reported

  WARNING: bad unlock balance detected!
  ... is trying to release lock (&ni->ni_lock) at:
  ntfs_readdir+0x2c6/0x600

on the first run, and so did a workload of 16 concurrent git worktrees
of one repository (run with a series of mine for resident files on
top of master).  With this patch applied on top of ee1cb3443cff the
directory test runs clean, and a 120 s run of 12 threads doing random
create/unlink/rename/link/mkdir/readdir/mmap/fallocate/fsync on four
shared directories reported no lockdep warnings.

Tested-by: Kamil Chojnowski <contact@diath.net>
